# Rust build artifacts
/target/
# Unanchored too: `crates/bevy_debugger_bevy` is a standalone package, not a workspace member,
# so building it directly creates its own target dir and lockfile beside it.
target/
crates/*/Cargo.lock
debug/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
**/mutants.out*/

# IDE files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db

# Logs and temporary files
*.log
logs/
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.temp

# Configuration files (keep examples)
config.toml
.env
.env.local

# Build artifacts
dist/
build/

# Coverage reports
tarpaulin-report.html
coverage/

# Local development
.claude/
claude_cache/

# macOS service files (runtime generated)
*.log.bak
.DS_Store

# Runtime session state written by the running server. These are checkpoints from a debugging
# session, not source: 16 of them were committed upstream, and because the monorepo mirrors this
# directory, simply running `bevy-debugger-mcp` dirtied the tree and tripped the clean-tree guard in
# `scripts/mirror_crates.sh` — blocking the mirror of every other crate too.
debug_sessions/
